.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt PWD 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pwd
.Nd print the process working directory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Print the working directory supplied by the process startup record,
or the runtime default
.Pa / .
The shell's
.Ic cd
builtin supplies that directory to commands it starts.
This command neither changes it nor enumerates filesystem authority.
Additional arguments are ignored; no physical/logical path options are
implemented.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the directory was obtained; 1 for a current-directory error,
diagnosed on standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pwd
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr absd-sh 1 ,
.Xr process 7
